FUNCTION acyclic_action_directive_relationship (relation : action_directive_relationship; relatives : SET [1:?] of action_directive; specific_relation : STRING):BOOLEAN;
	LOCAL
		x : SET of action_directive_relationship;
	END_LOCAL;
	IF relation.relating IN relatives THEN
		RETURN (FALSE);
	END_IF;
	x := QUERY(adr <* bag_to_set(USEDIN(relation.relating, 'ACTION_SCHEMA.' + 'ACTION_DIRECTIVE_RELATIONSHIP.' + 'RELATED')) | specific_relation IN TYPEOF(adr));
	REPEAT i := 1 TO HIINDEX(x);
		IF NOT acyclic_action_directive_relationship(x[i], relatives + relation.relating, specific_relation) THEN
	 		RETURN (FALSE);
		END_IF;
	END_REPEAT;
	RETURN (TRUE);
END_FUNCTION;


(*"acyclic_action_directive_relationship"
The *acyclic_action_directive_relationship* function determines whether the graph of instance of the entity data type
express_ref:[action_schema.action_directive]
that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle.
this function may be used to evaluate either a
express_ref:[action_schema.action_directive_relationship]
or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.


NOTE: The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.

*)

(*"acyclic_action_directive_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate
express_ref:[action_schema.action_directive_relationship]
to be checked.
*)

(*"acyclic_action_directive_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type
express_ref:[action_schema.action_directive]
for which the function is searching in the
express_ref:[action_schema.action_directive_relationship.relating]
parameter of the relation argument.
*)

(*"acyclic_action_directive_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the
express_ref:[action_schema.action_directive_relationship]
entity.
*)
